    "text":  "National University of Computer \u0026 Emerging Sciences - NUCES - Karachi Department of Artificial Intelligence 2.3 Wavelet Packet Transform (WPT) Mathematical Function: Wavelet packet transform is an extension of the DWT that allows for more flexible decomposition of signals. It decomposes signals into multiple subbands. Applications: WPT can be used for analyzing signals with complex frequency content and for feature extraction in machine learning. 2.4 Inverse Wavelet Transform Mathematical Function: To reconstruct a signal or image from its wavelet coefficients, an inverse wavelet transform is applied. It uses the original data along with the transformed coefficients to reconstruct the original signal. Applications : Inverse wavelet transforms are crucial for signal and image reconstruction in applications like image compression and de- noising. FAST NUCES - Karachi Talha Shahid 4",
